  {
   "id": 32,
   "type": "row",
   "title": "What each thing means",
   "collapsed": false,
   "gridPos": {
    "x": 0,
    "y": 74,
    "w": 24,
    "h": 1
   },
   "panels": []
  },
  {
   "id": 33,
   "type": "text",
   "title": "",
   "gridPos": {
    "x": 0,
    "y": 75,
    "w": 24,
    "h": 9
   },
   "options": {
    "mode": "markdown",
    "content": "| Term | Meaning |\n|---|---|\n| **Probe** | A tiny marker plugin placed before and after each guardrail. It notes the time and a hash of the body, nothing else. |\n| **Trail** | The list of probes a request passed. Where the trail stops is where the request was blocked. |\n| **Gap** | The space between two neighbouring probes. One gap holds one guardrail, so time spent in the gap is that guardrail's latency. |\n| **Reached** | Requests that got as far as this guardrail. Later guardrails see fewer, because earlier ones already stopped some. |\n| **Stopped or altered** | (blocked + rewritten) divided by reached, for one guardrail. |\n| **Chain share** | How much of the gateway's own time is spent in the guardrail chain. |\n| **Window** | All live numbers cover the last few minutes (`PASSIVE_WINDOW_S`), then slide forward. |\n| **Finding** | A short plain-language note written by Claude from the aggregates only. No prompts or responses are sent. |\n"
   },
   "transparent": true
  }
 ]
